Short:        Open-source TCP/IP stack, AmigaOS 3.1+
Author:       Laine Jones
Uploader:     Laine Jones (UPLOADER-EMAIL)
Type:         comm/tcp
Version:      @VER@
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.1.0
Requires:     a SANA-II network driver
Distribution: Aminet
URL:          https://github.com/lainejones/PrismNet

PrismNet is a free, open-source TCP/IP stack for classic Amigas: AmigaOS 3.1
or newer, any 68000 or better. It connects the Amiga to your network and the
internet through any SANA-II network driver, and provides the same
bsdsocket.library as AmiTCP, Miami and Roadshow, so the network programs you
already have - web browsers, wget, FTP, IRC, mail - run unchanged. The
networking core is lwIP 2.2.1.

What you get
------------
- bsdsocket.library (the AmiTCP 4 API, plus the Roadshow extensions newer
  programs use) and usergroup.library.
- The PrismNet command: START, STOP, STATUS, NETSTAT, ROUTE, ARP, LOG,
  SETCLOCK.
- PrismNet Prefs: network cards, DHCP or fixed addresses, DNS, routes,
  users, network shares and servers. It can import a Roadshow setup.
- PrismMon: addresses, traffic, open connections, memory and the log, live.
- DHCP, DNS (with mDNS for name.local), the clock from the network (SNTP),
  NetBIOS and mDNS names so other computers find the Amiga by name.
- Network shares (optional): an NFS export or an SMB 2/3 share (Windows,
  macOS, a NAS, Samba) as an ordinary Amiga volume, signing and encryption
  included.
- Servers (optional): FTP, telnet and web, started on demand by inetd.
- Serial links: built-in SLIP over serial.device, or any SANA-II
  point-to-point driver.
- An update check (68020+ with AmiSSL 5): PrismNet Prefs tells you when a
  newer PrismNet is out and can install it.
- WHDLoad games: the installer can switch the network off while a game runs
  and back on when you quit it (some games hang otherwise).
- Tools: ping, traceroute, nslookup, httpbench.
- An AmigaGuide manual.

Memory is taken as needed within a budget: about 290 KB while running, or
about 175 KB with the small core for 1-2 MB machines (the installer offers
it).

Requirements
------------
- AmigaOS 3.1 or newer, any 68000 or better.
- A SANA-II driver for your network hardware in DEVS:Networks (an Ethernet
  card, a PCMCIA card, a SCSI DaynaPORT, an A314, ...), or a serial port.

Installing
----------
Unpack the archive and double-click Install_PrismNet. It installs the
libraries, the PrismNet command, PrismNet Prefs, PrismMon and the manual,
and asks for your network driver and DHCP or a fixed address. Another
stack's libraries and tools are saved in C:Backup, and "Remove PrismNet"
puts them back. The installer asks all its questions first; updating keeps
your settings and takes the network away for only a few seconds.

Tested on
---------
Amiga 4000 (68060, ZZ9000 Ethernet), Amiga 2000 (68030, X-Surf), Amiga 1200
(68030, A314 and ZuluSCSI DaynaPORT), Amiga 500 (68030, BlueSCSI
DaynaPORT), CD32 (68030, built-in SLIP at 115200 baud), and WinUAE.

Source and help
---------------
Source, manual and issues: https://github.com/lainejones/PrismNet
Please report problems with the output of "PrismNet STATUS" and
"PrismNet LOG".

Thanks
------
The lwIP authors (Adam Dunkels, the Swedish Institute of Computer Science
and the lwIP contributors). The SMB and NFS clients are written from the
public specifications.

